\tag{discrete}

\import{discrete-macros}

\p{Some of the algebraic laws we learned are only valid in classical logic, and not in constructive logic.  For example:}
\ul{
  \li{The law of \em{excluded middle}, which says that #{P \lor \neg P \equiv \True}.  The problem is that XXX}
  \li{The \em{double negation} law, #{\neg \neg P \equiv P}}
  \li{One direction of de Morgan}
}
